    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1305">

                <pb facs="1037" n="921" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg921"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.77/124.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>It is impossible to do anything in the railway situation. The situation has been
                    further aggravated by the railway management’s refusal to give the men service
                    letters or transportation to the border. I have asked Mr. Calero to express to
                    the President this Embassy’s deep concern. I will be glad to be instructed to
                    take active steps to secure just treatment for the men. Shall I sign a general
                    certificate attesting the service of these men and their reason for leaving the
                    National Railways service?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
